# JuhRadial MX - device access for the logged-in user (systemd-logind uaccess)
#
# 73-seat-late.rules turns the uaccess tag into an ACL for the user of the
# active seat when a device appears, so the tag has to be set before it runs.
# The same tags in 99-juhradialmx.rules come too late for that: logind still
# applies them when you log in, but a device that appears later in the session
# (a Bluetooth reconnect, Easy-Switch back to this computer, a receiver plugged
# in) got no ACL and needed the input group. With this file the MX devices work
# right after installing, before the next login.
#
# Logitech devices only, matched by the parent HID device name
# "<bus>:046D:<product>.<n>": bus 0003 is USB (receivers and cables), 0005 is
# Bluetooth, whose virtual uhid parents expose no idVendor attribute.
# 99-juhradialmx.rules keeps the input group grant, which macro recording and
# generic-mode mice need for devices of other makers.

SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0003:046D:*", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0005:046D:*", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", KERNELS=="0003:046D:*", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", KERNELS=="0005:046D:*", TAG+="uaccess"
